        "Environment": "\" Elysia viridis is a small green sea slug with iridescent spots that feeds on Codium fragile sp. and retains the seaweed\u2019s chloroplasts (site of photosynthesis within algal cells). Once eaten, the chloroplasts continue to function and are a source of energy to the sea slug.\"",
        "Carrier of other organisms?": "",
        "Human consumption": "flavor is similar to goose barnacles",
        "Medicinal": "\"sulfated polysaccharides (SPs). The administration of this type of compounds reduced the oxidative damage associated with diabetes mellitus and obesity in several animal models without any cytotoxic effect\"",
        "Risks + dangers": "",
        "usage within agriculture + products": "",
        "medicinal": "",
        "Flavor/Diet": "",
        "medicinal/health": "",
        "Flavor/Diet.1": "",
        "other": "",
        "Additional properties": "",
        " ": ""
    },
